{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OpaqueExchange","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/opaqueexchange"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OpaqueExchange\/close()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OpaqueExchange","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The handle is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"single-use","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the library consumes it in "},{"code":"finish","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whether that succeeds or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails. This class takes it out of a one-shot slot, so a second "},{"code":"finish","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" throws rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handing a dangling pointer across the ABI."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" releases an exchange the caller abandoned — a login started and never completed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift’s refcounting makes that prompt rather than eventual, which is the one place its object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"model is kinder here than a tracing GC’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"class"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"struct"},{"type":"text","text":" for exactly that reason: the release has to happen when the"},{"type":"tex